1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,330
One git clone could run a hacker's code on

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:03,191
your machine.

3
00:00:03,191 --> 00:00:04,551
This week, Git patched six

4
00:00:04,551 --> 00:00:05,511
vulnerabilities.

5
00:00:05,511 --> 00:00:07,958
The worst is rated high severity.

6
00:00:07,988 --> 00:00:08,908
Here's the trick.

7
00:00:08,908 --> 00:00:11,028
Before Git writes a file, it checks the

8
00:00:11,028 --> 00:00:13,268
path, so nothing can overwrite its own

9
00:00:13,268 --> 00:00:14,502
.git data.

10
00:00:14,512 --> 00:00:16,512
But the attacker uses an extremely

11
00:00:16,512 --> 00:00:17,232
long path.

12
00:00:17,232 --> 00:00:18,952
Its length gets truncated.

13
00:00:18,952 --> 00:00:20,432
So it passes the check under

14
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:22,232
its full name, then gets written

15
00:00:22,232 --> 00:00:24,464
under a shorter one: .git

16
00:00:24,474 --> 00:00:26,874
Inside a submodule, that file becomes

17
00:00:26,874 --> 00:00:28,394
a symlink, pointing at a

18
00:00:28,394 --> 00:00:30,206
folder of malicious hooks.

19
00:00:30,216 --> 00:00:31,456
When Git uses that folder,

20
00:00:31,456 --> 00:00:33,096
the attacker's code runs.

21
00:00:33,096 --> 00:00:35,696
On your laptop, or your CI runner.

22
00:00:35,726 --> 00:00:36,766
It only triggers with

23
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:39,166
--recurse-submodules, which pipelines and

24
00:00:39,166 --> 00:00:41,263
coding agents use all the time.

25
00:00:41,293 --> 00:00:44,333
The fix: update to Git 2.56.1,

26
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,939
or a patched backport.

27
00:00:45,949 --> 00:00:47,028
Can't update yet?

28
00:00:47,028 --> 00:00:48,949
Clone without submodules first,

29
00:00:48,949 --> 00:00:51,129
and inspect .gitmodules

30
00:00:51,199 --> 00:00:53,159
A repo is code from a stranger.

31
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:54,651
Treat it that way.

